@startuml
title Service Qualification & Feasibility Check

skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor<<blackbox>> Black
  ParticipantFontColor<<blackbox>> White
}

participant "Product Order\nOrchestration &\nManagement" as POOM <<blackbox>>
participant "Product Catalog\nManagement" as PCM <<blackbox>>
participant "Event Mgt" as EventMgt #grey
participant "Service Qualification\nManagement" as SQM #blue
participant "Service Catalog\nManagement" as SCM #blue
participant "Service Order\nManagement" as SOM #blue
participant "Service Inventory" as SI #blue
participant "Resource Order\nManagement" as ROM #blue

== Step 6-8 ==

POOM -> PCM : 1 **TMF620 Product Catalog Management**\nGET /productSpecification
activate PCM
PCM --> POOM : 2 **TMF620** 200 productSpecification details, CFSSpecification,\nresourceSpecification, //translationRules//
deactivate PCM

POOM -> SOM : 3 **TMF641 Service Ordering**\nPOST /serviceOrder (CFSSpecification)
activate SOM

== CSMF Responsibility ==

note over SOM : CSMF receives the CFS Order and CFS Specification\nfor Business Slice and Service Profile

SOM -> SOM : 4 validate CFS order\n(state="acknowledged")
SOM --> POOM : 5 **TMF641** 201 serviceOrder (state="acknowledged")

POOM -> POOM : 6 link productOrderItems and CFSOrderItems

note over SOM : CSMF starts execution of the CFS Order
SOM -> SOM : 7 start execution of CFSOrder

group execute CFSOrder orchestration sequence

    SOM -> SOM : 8 update CFSOrderItem (state="inProgress")

    SOM -> EventMgt : 9 **TMF688 Event Management**\nPOST event serviceOrderStateChange\n(serviceOrderItemState="inProgress")
    activate EventMgt
    EventMgt --> POOM : 10 **TMF688 Event Management**\nPOST listener/serviceOrderStateChange\n(serviceOrderItemState="inProgress")
    deactivate EventMgt

    note over SOM : CSMF initiates Service Qualification\nChecks Business Slice (type) eligibility\nat given location (address)for given party profile

    SOM -> SQM : 11 **TMF645 Service Qualification**\nPOST /serviceQualification (CFSSpecification)
    SQM --> SOM : 12 **TMF645** 201 serviceQualification

    note over SOM
      CSMF initiates Business Slice CFS feasibility check
      Feasibility of the Business slice is checked
      for available/reusable Service alternatives
      Additionally for Service Profile CFS, verifies
      feasibility (Quantitative Analysis)
    end note

    note over SOM : CSMF translates the Service Profile CFS Charecteristics\nto the corresponding Service Profile RFS requirements\nneeded for Network Slice RFS processing

    SOM -> SI : 13 **TMF638 Service Inventory Management**\nPOST /service (CFS) (state="feasibilityChecked")
    SI --> SOM : 14 **TMF638** 201 CFS

    note over SOM : CSMF deomposes CFS to corresponding RFS

    SOM -> SCM : 15 **TMF633 Service Catalog Management**\nGET /serviceSpecification (CFSSpecification)
    activate SCM
    SCM --> SOM : 16 **TMF633** 200 RFS Specification
    deactivate SCM

    SOM -> SOM : 17 decide between RFS alternatives

end

== NSMF Responsibility ==

note over SOM : NSMF initiates RFS feasibility check

SOM -> SI : 18 **TMF638 Service Inventory Management**\nPOST /service (Slice RFS, Service Profile RFS) (state="feasibilityChecked")

note over SOM : NSMF : Qualitative and Quantitative feasibility of Network Slice RFS and Service Profile RFS is checked

SI --> SOM : 19 **TMF638** 201 RFS

note over SOM : NSMF decomposes Network Slice RFS\nto Slice Subnet RFS (RAN/Core/Transport)

SOM -> SCM : 20 **TMF633 Service Catalog Management**\nGET /serviceSpecification (RFS Specification)
activate SCM
SCM --> SOM : 21 **TMF633** 200 RFS Specification
deactivate SCM

SOM -> SOM : 22 decide between RFS alternatives

note over SOM : NSMF translates the Service Profile RFS Charecteristics\nto the corresponding Slice Profile requirements\nneeded for Network Slice Subnet RFS processing

== NSSMF Responsibility ==

note over SOM : NSSMF initiates RFS feasibility check

SOM -> SI : 23 **TMF638 Service Inventory Management**\nPOST /service (Slice RFS, Slice Profile RFS) (state="feasibilityChecked")

note over SOM : NSSMF : Qualitative and Quantitative feasibility of Network Slice Subnet  RFS and Slice Profile RFS is checked

SI --> SOM : 24 **TMF638** 201 RFS

SOM -> SCM : 25 **TMF633 Service Catalog Management**\nGET /serviceSpecification (RFS Specification)
activate SCM
SCM --> SOM : 26 **TMF633** 200 resourceSpecification
deactivate SCM

note over SOM : NSSMF corresponding to each domain\nprepares resource order items
SOM -> SOM : 27 build **resourceOrderItems**

note over SOM : NSSMF initiates resource order fulfilment

SOM -> ROM : 28 **TMF652 Resource Ordering Management**\nPOST /resourceOrder
activate ROM
ROM -> ROM : 29 validate resourceOrder
ROM --> SOM : 30 **TMF652** 201 resourceOrder (state="acknowledged")

ROM -> ROM : 31 start execution of\nresourceOrder
deactivate ROM

SOM -> SOM : 32 link serviceOrderItem and **resourceOrderItems**
deactivate SOM

@enduml
